      "confidence": 0.95,
      "evidence": [
        "artifacts/ae_ip_by_year.csv shows extreme year-to-year swings with expected counts ~1,000–2,000, vastly exceeding 1/sqrt(E) Poisson noise",
        "overall A/E=0.9995 confirms stable central level despite high dispersion",
        "artifacts/ae_ip_termination.csv shows termination rates near 1.00, ruling out a recovery-driven claim count shift"
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Investigate data quality and reporting practices (e.g., accident vs policy year misalignment, reporting lag, IBNR methodology). Review claim size distribution for outsized single/group claim clustering. Adjust credibility weighting and reserve models to account for overdispersion (e.g., negative binomial); do not use Poisson-based z-scores for this book."
    }
  ]
}

